## Control Center final integration candidate

Final integration and release-qualification branch for the Morro Digital Control Center.

### Integrated state
The current branch is reconciled with main `1cc6fe4f7fe4fb4074890a435a54ac191fde4c8e` and contains the completed Control Center waves, including:
- UX Design V1 (#219);
- reusable responsive/accessibility primitives (#227);
- destination-aware Universal Search (#228);
- Entity 360 / Dashboard / Recent Activity (#229, plus post-main reconciliation #235);
- owner-backed real-data aggregates (#230);
- deterministic visual regression and documentation ledger (#231);
- the latest main-side UX V2 and staging Control Center bootstrap changes through #236.

### Exact-head candidate
`287d6d6bf7fbdef874c7085dad01334f21188909`

This head includes an isolated CI-harness correction so the Control Center browser contract boots the canonical Destination owner against its MySQL service via `DESTINATIONS_DATABASE_URL`. This preserves the fail-closed owner-backed destination invariant instead of accepting a synthetic DOM-only destination.

### Current qualification
- PR is currently mergeable and 0-behind the captured base;
- exact-head CI is running on the SHA above;
- Dependency Security Audit and multiple exact-head contracts are already green;
- final certification remains pending until all required/relevant exact-head workflows complete successfully;
- no previous-head CI result is reused as certification evidence.

### Invariants
- no Quick Actions;
- no floating Assistant launcher;
- `destinationId` is explicit and owner-backed;
- unknown/non-owner destination IDs fail closed to global/unavailable semantics rather than being inferred;
- affiliates remain platform-owned;
- Support Mode preserves actor/effectiveUser separation, step-up, reason, confirmation and append-only audit;
- authorization remains server-side;
- Financial remains monetary authority;
- no production deployment, destructive migration, refund, payout or irreversible data operation is part of this integration PR.

### Concurrent development
PR #237 currently targets staging credential bootstrap files only and has no file overlap with this PR. If it or any other PR moves main before final certification, this branch must be reconciled and affected evidence re-run before merge.

