Moves the generated tree from `openapi-v237.2.0` to `openapi-v239.10.0`. Generated with `PROTOCOL_REF=latest melos run gen:openapi`; the diff is confined to `lib/open_api/`, plus the plan tables `generate_plan.py` rebuilds from it.

## Why now

Group 08 (Moderation & Blocklists) is blocked on this spec in two places, and both clear with the newer one.

`unban` now exists as an operation, so `banUser` and `unbanUser` can move together instead of leaving the pair half-migrated:

```dart
@POST('/api/v2/moderation/unban')
Future<Result<UnbanResponse>> unban({
  @Query('target_user_id') required String targetUserId,
  @Query('channel_cid') String? channelCid,
});
```

And `QueryBannedUsersPayload` gained the four `created_at_*` cursors. The server reads them off an embedded `*types.BansPager` in `GetPager()`, but the older spec did not flatten that embed — so routing `queryBannedUsers` through the generated client would have dropped `created_at_after`, `created_at_after_or_equal`, `created_at_before` and `created_at_before_or_equal` without a compile error.

## Other changes in the spec bump

`CreateReminderResponse`, `TranslateMessageResponse` and `UnbanResponse` are back after a14211740 removed them. That commit dropped them because they were generated, exported by nothing and returned by no operation; this time operations return all three. `createReminder` is retyped from `ReminderResponseData`, `translateMessage` from `MessageActionResponse`, and `BanRequest` loses the server-side-only `banned_by` / `banned_by_id`.

All three belong to groups that have not migrated yet (06 Reminders, 10 Messages, 08 Moderation), so no publicly exported symbol changes and there is no Symbol Map row or CHANGELOG entry to add. The four generated types already exposed by landed migrations — `Role`, `SearchRolesResponse`, `ListDevicesResponse`, `CreateDeviceRequest` — are byte-identical.

